Subject: [PATCH 19/23] sheet route: the cut face is a port (skin coupling),
 cut-face trace deliverable, Gmsh manifold check

The cut surface carries load (a skin is attached to it), so it is a port like the box faces: the cut cap is built on
the cut_0 carrier trace, the mesh adapter classifies cut facets as cut_0 and P interpolates them on that trace, the
cut-face active set is the geometric triangle rule, a fragment attached to the cut face alone is kept, the rotation
check matches carrier nodes by exact coordinates, and the contract domain says so. The block validation constrains
the block's cut cap to the union of the cells' cut traces and ties its fine nodes in the constrained control.

Gmsh Delaunay produced a volume mesh with 31 nonmanifold facets on a sliver-rich cut cap (pop_cut_0003, up to 14
tetrahedra per facet); the cut caps are no worse than the box caps (59 cells), so mesh_sheet_solid now counts
nonmanifold volume facets, rejects such a mesh itself and retries once with HXT (the existing crash retry), and the
receipt records algorithm3d and nonmanifold_facets.

Deliverable of the coupling contract: every label directory, PASS or EMPTY, writes CUT_FACE_TRACE.npz, the cell's
cut_0 trace in world coordinates with global keys; the union over a block is one conforming triangulation of the cut
plane (2x1x1 cut block: 3182 nodes, 0 key/coordinate conflicts, every edge in 2 triangles except the outer boundary).

Results: pop_cut_0003 / pop_cut_0623 / tilt60_mid PASS with q 8868 / 4224 / 6804 (x1.25 to x1.51 over the free cut),
rigid residual <= 1.9e-13; 2x1x1 cut block assembled vs constrained monolithic 4.0e-4 (tension) to 1.25e-2 (4H),
interface mismatch 0. STEP6 report added. merge_cut_carrier refuses a second application.

